# mTCP config for a dosbridge client. STATIC on purpose.
#
# Do not run DHCP.EXE against this file. It is one-shot: it stamps
# TIMESTAMP and LEASE_TIME in here and exits, nothing renews the lease,
# and when it expires every mTCP tool refuses to run. The agent loop
# cannot recover from that on its own -- its offline branch retries
# forever but never re-runs DHCP -- so it costs a trip to the box.
#
# The bridge does not read this file at all any more: it reads
# C:\AI\NET.CFG. This exists only for mTCP's own tools,
# so if you have no mTCP you can ignore it entirely.
#
packetint 0x60
hostname DOSBOX

IPADDR 192.168.1.20
NETMASK 255.255.255.0
GATEWAY 192.168.1.1
NAMESERVER 192.168.1.1
MTU 1500
